## NVIDIA GPU Drivers

To add the optional NVIDIA GPU driver to the compute nodes, an additional
external {{ pkg_manager }} repository provided by NVIDIA must be configured.
Once the repository is configured, the GPU driver needs to be installed on the
compute image and the corresponding toolkit installed on the head node.

OpenHPC provides a convenience package to enable the NVIDIA repository locally
along with compatibility packages that integrate the NVIDIA HPC SDK within the
standard OpenHPC user environment.

::: {.tip}
**Note:** The driver is NVIDIA's open GPU kernel module
(`kmod-nvidia-open-dkms`), which supports GPUs of the Turing architecture and
newer. {% if is_el %}NVIDIA's EL{{ distro_version }} repository offers it as the
`nvidia-driver:open-dkms` module stream, which the recipe enables before the
install; the `nvidia-driver:latest-dkms` stream holds the proprietary module
for older GPUs.{% endif %}
:::

<!-- ohpc_begin -->
<!-- ohpc_if_set enable_nvidia_gpu_driver -->
```bash
# Add NVIDIA GPU driver repository to the head node
{{ head_install("cuda-repo-ohpc") }}

# Add NVIDIA GPU driver repository to the compute nodes
{{ compute_install("cuda-repo-ohpc") }}
{%- if is_el %}

# Select the open kernel module stream (EL{{ distro_version }} uses DNF modules)
{{ compute_run("dnf -y module enable nvidia-driver:open-dkms") }}
{%- endif %}

# Install the GPU driver on the compute nodes
{{ compute_install(["nvidia-driver-cuda", "kmod-nvidia-open-dkms"]) }}

# Build the driver for the image's kernel (DKMS otherwise targets the running kernel)
{{ compute_run("dkms autoinstall -k \\$(ls /lib/modules | sort -V | tail -n 1)") }}

# Enable DKMS service to automatically rebuild driver
{{ compute_run("systemctl enable dkms") }}

# Install the toolkit on the head node
{{ head_install("cuda-devel-ohpc") }}
```
<!-- ohpc_fi -->
<!-- ohpc_end -->
